screens.text_md:
Rust inserts `deref` calls when the types line up in one of three ways:

- from `&T` to `&U` when `T: Deref<Target = U>`;
- from `&mut T` to `&mut U` when `T: DerefMut<Target = U>`;
- from `&mut T` to `&U` when `T: Deref<Target = U>`.

The third rule turns a mutable reference into a shared one, which is always safe. The reverse never happens: a shared reference can't become a mutable one, because there might be other shared references to the same data.

