screens.text_md:
Use `Rc<T>` when one value really has several owners and you can't tell at compile time which will finish last: nodes in a graph, a shared configuration, the tail two lists both continue with.

Keep in mind:

- it's single-threaded (the compiler stops you sending it to another thread);
- `Rc::clone` is cheap, a count increase, not a data copy;
- values in an `Rc` can't be changed through it;
- two `Rc`s pointing at each other never reach a count of zero (L15.7).

