    out
}

problems.description_md:
Build a family forest. `forest(names, parents)` makes one `Person` per name. `parents[i]` names person `i`'s parent: `Some(p)` with `p < i` makes `p` the parent (parents own children strongly; a child refers to its parent weakly), and `None` or `Some(p)` with `p >= i` makes `i` a root. Allowing only earlier parents makes cycles impossible.

Return:

- the names of the roots, sorted;
- for every person in input order, the path from the root down to them, names joined with `/` (`"ana/bo/cy"`);
- whether every person is freed after all the handles `forest` holds are dropped (check with weak handles taken beforehand).

